Q1. What is the Proxy Design Pattern?
Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

The Proxy Pattern is a
Structural Design Pattern
that provides a placeholder
or surrogate for another object
to control access to it.

The client communicates
with the Proxy,

and the Proxy decides
whether and when to
forward the request
to the real object.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need Proxy Pattern?

• Control access to objects.
• Improve Security.
• Perform Authentication.
• Perform Authorization.
• Implement Lazy Loading.
• Add Logging.
• Add Caching.
• Access Remote Objects.

------------------------------------------------------------

How does it work?

Client

↓

Proxy

↓

Real Object

The Proxy performs checks such as

• Authentication
• Authorization
• Logging
• Caching

After the checks,

it forwards the request
to the real object.

------------------------------------------------------------

Real-Life Example

ATM Machine

Customer

↓

ATM (Proxy)

↓

Bank Server

The ATM verifies

• PIN
• Card
• Balance

before communicating
with the Bank Server.

------------------------------------------------------------

Software Industry Example

Application

↓

Security Proxy

↓

Database

The Security Proxy checks
whether the user has
permission before allowing
access to the Database.

