Q2. Difference between Proxy Pattern
and Decorator Pattern

Interview Ready Answer

Proxy Pattern

• Structural Design Pattern.
• Controls access to
  an existing object.
• Focuses on Security,
  Authentication,
  Authorization,
  Logging,
  Caching,
  Lazy Loading.
• May allow or deny access
  after performing checks.

------------------------------------------------------------

Decorator Pattern

• Structural Design Pattern.
• Adds new functionality
  to an existing object.
• Focuses on adding
  responsibilities dynamically.
• Does not control access.

------------------------------------------------------------

Examples

Decorator

Coffee

↓

MilkDecorator

↓

SugarDecorator

↓

ChocolateDecorator

Each decorator adds
a new feature.

------------------------------------------------------------

Proxy

Client

↓

SecurityProxy

↓

Database

The Proxy authenticates
the user before forwarding
the request.

------------------------------------------------------------

